@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# XPress Serving in vLLM — Reproduction Guide
+
+This fork adds **XPress** (K-pass parallel Jacobi refinement over a DFlash
+block drafter) as
+first-class V1 speculative-decoding methods. Base: upstream `main` @ 82ae416.
+
+## What's in the branch (`xpress-serving`)
+
+| Path | Role |
+|---|---|
+| `vllm/model_executor/models/xpress_head.py` | pure-torch refiner head (importable w/o vLLM; mixer folded at load; candidate-restricted `jacobi_refine_greedy`) |
+| `vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3_xpress.py` | `Qwen3XPressForCausalLM` (shares target embed/lm_head; DFlash 5-layer backbone) |
+| `vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/xpress/` | `XPressSpeculator` (K loop-free Jacobi passes, CUDA-graph captured) + fused-kernel experiment (off by default; documented negative result) |
+| small edits | registration in `config/speculative.py`, `models/registry.py`, `spec_decode/__init__.py`, model runner |
+| `docs/xpress/specdec_bench_harness.patch` | 37-line patch adding `XPRESS` to NVIDIA SpecDec-Bench (`TensorRT-Model-Optimizer/examples/specdec_bench`) |
+
+## Environment (verified: H200, driver >= CUDA 12.x)
+
+```bash
+conda create -n vllm-xpress python=3.11 -y && conda activate vllm-xpress
+git clone -b xpress-serving https://github.com/ZKBig/vllm.git && cd vllm
+# Python-only changes on a recent base -> use the prebuilt wheel for the base commit:
+VLLM_USE_PRECOMPILED=1 pip install -e .
+# If the node's driver is older than the wheel's CUDA, prepend the compat layer:
+#   export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/cuda-13.0/compat:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
+export FLASHINFER_DISABLE_VERSION_CHECK=1
+```
+
+## Checkpoints
+
+Serving checkpoints (converted format, `Qwen3XPressForCausalLM` architectures):
+
+```bash
+hf download VictorZheng/Qwen3-8B-XPress-b16-consis-k3 --local-dir ckpts/Qwen3-8B-XPress-b16
+```
+
+Key config fields: `xpress_num_passes: 6`, `xpress_fused_kernel: false`;
+`xpress_candidate_topc` must be **0 or absent** (full-vocab, exact semantics —
+the release default). ALWAYS check
+`xpress_num_passes` before benchmarking — it is a run knob living in config.json.
+
+## Run the benchmark
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-Model-Optimizer && cd TensorRT-Model-Optimizer
+git apply /path/to/vllm/docs/xpress/specdec_bench_harness.patch
+cd examples/specdec_bench
+python run.py \
+  --model_dir Qwen/Qwen3-8B --tokenizer Qwen/Qwen3-8B \
+  --draft_model_dir /path/to/ckpts/Qwen3-8B-XPress-b16 \
+  --mtbench question.jsonl --engine VLLM --speculative_algorithm XPRESS \
+  --block_size 15 --tp_size 1 --ep_size 1 --output_length 2048 \
+  --concurrency 1 --show_progress
+```
+
+## Expected results (Qwen3-8B, H200, T=0)
+
+- MT-Bench bs=1: AL ~3.84, ~560 tok/s (drafter 2.98/455, DSpark 3.71/529)
+- SPEED 1k c32: AL ~3.43, ~4590 tok/s; 8k c32: step time ~= bare drafter
+  (refinement overhead -> 0 at long context), +18% TPS vs drafter
+- Cross-node tolerance: AL +-0.05; absolute tok/s varies by node — compare
+  same-session pairs or ratios only.
+
+## Design notes
+
+- Default scoring is FULL-VOCAB (exact semantics; all published numbers).
+  `xpress_candidate_topc: 256` is an opt-in speedup (~10x less readout traffic,
+  measured AL-neutral) but restricts the per-pass argmax to the drafter's
+  top-C, so it is deliberately NOT the release default.
+- The whole draft step (backbone + K passes) is FULL-CUDA-graph captured;
+  a hand-fused persistent Triton kernel was measured SLOWER than graphed torch
+  at bs=1 (single-block = 1 SM) and is kept only as a documented negative
+  result (`spec_decode/xpress/kernels.py`, flag default off).
+- T=0 only in this fork; the lossless T>0 (frozen-Gumbel honest-q) machinery
+  lives in the research harness.
